# =============================================================================
# Trivy CONTAINER IMAGE ignores (deliberately separate from .trivyignore).
# =============================================================================
# Consumed by .github/workflows/deploy.yml (`build` job):
#   trivy image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL --exit-code 1 \
#     --ignore-unfixed --ignorefile .trivyignore.images <repo>@sha256:...
#
# WHY A SECOND FILE
# -----------------
# .trivyignore holds Terraform MISCONFIGURATION accepts (AVD-AWS-*) consumed by
# `trivy config` in ci.yml. Image scanning consumes CVE identifiers
# (CVE-*/GHSA-*), a disjoint namespace with a completely different review
# cadence: an infrastructure accept is a standing architectural decision, while
# a CVE suppression is a temporary, dated waiver that should disappear when the
# fix ships. Mixing them in one file makes both impossible to audit.
#
# THE SCAN IS BLOCKING. A HIGH/CRITICAL finding with an available fix fails the
# build, and the image is therefore never deployed (the `deploy` job needs
# `build`). `--ignore-unfixed` already excludes findings this pipeline cannot
# action, so anything that lands here is a CVE that COULD be fixed by rebuilding
# or bumping a dependency and is being consciously deferred.
#
# RULES FOR ADDING AN ENTRY
#   1. One CVE/GHSA id per line.
#   2. A comment above it: which image, why it is not exploitable here (or what
#      compensating control applies), who accepted it, and an expiry date.
#   3. Prefer `exp:` so trivy re-raises the finding automatically when the
#      waiver lapses — a suppression with no end date becomes permanent by
#      accident. Format:  CVE-2026-12345 exp:2026-12-31
#   4. Fix it instead, if a fix exists. This file is the exception path.
#
# Currently EMPTY: no image CVE waivers are in force. If the first enforced run
# fails, triage the findings — bump the base image or the dependency — and only
# add an entry here when a fix genuinely is not available yet.
# =============================================================================
